<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erridupizir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">22nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Erridu-pizir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erridupizir was a Gutian king who ruled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in the 22nd century BCE, after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. He is known from copies of his inscriptions found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a>, in which he took the Akkadian title 'king of the four quarters' and recorded campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lullubi">Lullubi</a>. He is not named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a>.</p></div>
